  "id": "split-stance-squat",
  "name": "Stationary Split Squat",
  "definition": "A stationary unilateral-emphasis compound exercise performed from a fixed sagittal split stance. The roster owns a floor-supported split squat and the directly reviewed high-bar rear-foot-elevated fixture; both keep their contacts fixed and return through lead-side hip extension, knee extension, and ankle plantarflexion. The elevated branch pins rear support to base-of-patella height and individualizes stance from the lead patella-over-toe relationship at the reviewed depth. Dynamic lunges, unsupported rear-foot variants, other elevations, Smith, dumbbell, kettlebell, bodyweight, and deficit branches remain outside this contract.",
