      "execution": {
        "startingPosition": "Set a stable rear box to the bottom-of-kneecap height, secure the rear foot against its posterior stop, place the lead leg in line with that hip, and hold the bar high on the upper back.",
        "movement": "Lower with both contacts fixed until the lead knee reaches approximately ninety degrees and the kneecap is aligned over the lead toe.",
        "endpoint": "Reach the individualized reviewed depth without changing the foot positions or rear support.",
        "returnPhase": "Rise through the lead hip, knee, and ankle without stepping between repetitions.",
        "controlledJoints": "Keep the lead knee tracking with the foot and do not let the rear foot slide.",
        "supportAndPosture": "Maintain the high-bar position while the unreported trunk angle remains consistent across the set.",
        "disqualifyingCompensations": ["Losing or sliding the rear-foot support changes the reviewed fixture.", "Stepping or drifting from the individualized stance changes the stationary split squat."],
